# The setup menu's keys, one each, as a user presses them: [P] toggles the
# printer and [A] the paper, each shown at once; [T] takes the idle timeout
# typed in (30), and refuses one out of range (999); [O] takes a new folder
# (/JOBS); [E] starts the printer. A job printed then (our ESC/P pages, sent
# by PRFILES) lands in the new folder as a PDF, the one tools/printer/render
# writes for it, the folder made at the job.
@disk-a tools/dev/builds/disks/escp.st
text "Machine +: (ST|STE|Mega STE), TOS" 1500
key p
text "\[P\]rinter +: HP LaserJet II" 300
key p
text "\[P\]rinter +: Epson FX-80" 300
key a
text "P\[a\]per +: Letter" 300
key a
text "P\[a\]per +: A4" 300
key t
text "Seconds of quiet that end a job" 300
type 30
key 0x1c
text "\[T\]imeout +: 30 s" 300
key t
type 999
key 0x1c
text "\[T\]imeout +: 30 s" 300
key o
text "The folder for the PDFs" 300
type /JOBS
key 0x1c
text "F\[o\]lder +: /JOBS" 300
key e
text "Starting the printer" 300
wait 100
key 0x01
wait 900
key 0x39
log "pages: job 00000001 rendered, 3 pages, PDF 32366 bytes" 6000
cardsame JOBS/00000001.pdf tools/dev/builds/disks/escp-expected.pdf
cardnone PRINTER/00000001.pdf
